# Build context for the ROOT Dockerfile, which builds ONLY the Flask backend
# (`gunicorn --chdir pipeline app:app`). Without this file the root `COPY . .`
# put the ENTIRE monorepo into the backend image: 443 MB of git-tracked files
# for a service whose runtime footprint is about 1 MB.
#
# The excluded directories are not "probably unused" -- each is either a
# separate deployable with its own Dockerfile, or non-code. Verified 2026-08-26
# by importing pipeline/app.py and listing sys.modules: the Flask app loads 33
# deal_intelligence modules and none of them read anything outside
# deal_intelligence/*.py and deal_intelligence/prompts/.
#
# deal_intelligence/data/ is deliberately NOT excluded. It is only 5.4 MB, and
# the one-off Cloud Run Job scripts (backfill_deal_dates.py,
# backfill_hub_deal_dates.py) read deal-date-corrections-2026-08-14.json out of
# it. Those jobs run from this same image, so dropping the directory to save
# 1.2% of the context would break them for no meaningful gain.

# ── Separate deployables: each has its own Dockerfile + Cloud Run service ────
hub-next/
hub/
cc-attio-sync/

# ── Non-code: decks, brand assets, planning docs, one-off analysis ──────────
higgsfield/
design/
docs/
scripts/
n8n-cloudrun/
gmail-attio-scripts/
lp-screener/
takeover-notes/

# ── Tests: run in CI / locally, never needed in the runtime image ───────────
deal_intelligence/tests/
pipeline/tests/
pytest.ini
requirements-dev.txt

# ── Local I/O folders (contents are gitignored; the dirs hold only .gitkeep) ─
pipeline/Documents/
pipeline/attio_import/
deal_intelligence/output/

# ── VCS / tooling / local environments ──────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.claude/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
*.swp
.env
.env.*
README.md
